NOTE on libratbag-data.c
================================================================

The ATK driver does NOT need any init_data_atk() function in
libratbag-data.c — it has no per-device data sections in the
.device files (unlike sinowealth which has [Driver/sinowealth/devices/X]
sections). The simple Driver=atk line is enough.

The driver_id_map[] in libratbag-data.c (around line 513) maps
driver string names to enum values. We need to add ATK there.

Check the enum and map:
  grep -n "SINOWEALTH\|ETEKCITY\|driver_id_map\|enum.*driver" src/libratbag-data.c | head -20
  grep -n "SINOWEALTH\|ETEKCITY" src/libratbag-data.h | head -20

Then add:
  - ATK to the driver enum in libratbag-data.h
  - { ATK, "atk", NULL } to driver_id_map[] in libratbag-data.c

